leans Office Of Admissions Test Information IN THIS SECTION Office of Admissions Information for Accepted Students Meet Your Counselors Visit Us Apply to LSU New Orleans Important Dates and Deadlines Tuition and Fees Transcripts Test Information Privateer Enrollment Center Contact Us Site Translation Test Information Directions Accuplacer Test LSU New Orleans recognizes that taking either the SAT or ACT at this time may be challenging. LSU New Orleans will admit in-state freshmen who apply with a minimum 2.5+ GPA or greater on the Louisiana Core 4. Applicants with a 2.5+ core GPA who do not meet test score requirements, or do not submit test scores will be admitted based on core GPA alone, but will either need to submit the test scores they have or sit for an accuplacer exam for English and Math placement purposes. For any questions please contact the Privateer Enrollment Center at [email protected] . American College Test (ACT) If you are a freshman or transfer applicant who has completed less than 24 semester hours of college coursework, you must take the ACT (American College Test) and have your scores sent to LSU New Orleans (college code 1591). National ACT tests are administered in October, December, February, April, and June each year at regular ACT testing centers. Scholastic Aptitude Test (SAT I) The SAT I (Scholastic Aptitude Test, LSU New Orleans college code 6379) may be used in place of the ACT. Test dates are in October, November, December, January, April, May, and June. Freshmen Test Requirements Transfer Test Requirements International Test Requirements Test Placement LSU New Orleans offers opportunities to receive course credit and placement based on standardized test scores. Be sure that your most up-to-date information is on file with LSU New Orleans in order to be placed into the corresponding courses below. Test Placement Course AP ACT SAT Accuplacer Compass ENGL 1157 -- English = 18 SAT ERW = 500 - 639 Sentence Skills = 86 Writing skills = 70 ENGL 1158 Engl Lang = 3 English = 28-31 SAT ERW = 640 - 699 SAT Reading = 33-37 SAT Critical Reading = 450 - 619 NextGen => 270 & 1157 ASA Sentence Skills => 100 & 1157 ASA > = 90 & 1157 ASA ENGL comp exemption Engl Lang = > 4 English = > 32 & 1158 ASA SAT ERW => 700 and 1158 ASA SAT Reading => 38 and 1158 ASA SAT Critical Reading => 620 Successful ENGL 1157 ASA & 1158 ASA Successful ENGL 1157 ASA & 1158 ASA MATH 1021: Problem Solving and Number Relations for Elem Teachers -- Math = 19 SAT Math = 500 NextGen:QRAS =>250 Elementary Algebra => 65 Algebra = > 40 MATH 1023: Problem Solving and Geometry for Elem Teachers -- Math = 19 SAT Math = 500 NextGen:QRAS =>250 Elementary Algebra => 65 Algebra = > 40 MATH 1031: Survey of Mathematical Thought I -- Math = 19 SAT Math = 500 NextGen:QRAS =>250 Elementary Algebra => 65 Algebra = > 40 MATH 1032: Survey of Mathematical Thought II -- Math = 19 SAT Math = 500 NextGen:QRAS =>250 Elementary Algebra => 65 Algebra = > 40 MATH 1115: Applied Algebra -- Math = 19 SAT Math = 500 NextGen:QRAS =>250 Elementary Algebra => 65 Algebra = > 40 MATH 1125: Precalculus Algebra -- Math = 22 SAT Math = 550 NextGen:AAF =>250 College Level Math => 63 Algebra = > 66 MATH 1126: Precalculus Trig -- Math = 26 SAT Math = 610 NextGen:AAF =>263 College Level Math => 86 Coll Algebra = > 46 MATH 2114: Calculus I Calculus AB = > 3 Math = 28 SAT Math = 650 NextGen:AAF =>276 College Level Math =>103 Trig = > 46 MATH 2124: Calculus II Calculus AB = > 4 Calculus BC = > 3 MATH 2134: Calculus III Calculus BC = 5 ALEKS PPL (LSU Baton Rouge results only) Score Placement 81 or higher Math 2114 Honors section 76 or higher Math 2114 61 or higher Math 1126 35 or higher Math 1125 Resources American College Test (ACT) College Board TOEFL Educational Testing Services (ETS) ALEKS PPL Footer Contact 2000 Lakeshore Drive New Orleans, LA 70148 [email protected] [email protected] +1 (888) 514-4275 +1 (888) 514-4275 +1 (504) 384-7924 +1 (504) 384-7924 Learn Admission information Programs of study Scholarships and awards Tuition and fees Graduate programs Financial aid Important dates & deadlines Experience International center Our campus Student life Housing Career services Alumni Make a gift Annual Security Report Connect All social University calendar News For parents Espanol - Tieng Viet Privacy Policy Accessibility Non-Discrimination Title IX Campus Crime Emergency Preparedness © 2026 LSU New Orleans. All Rights Reserved."
